1
00:00:00,700 --> 00:00:04,884
The air conditioning was broken.
Twelve people sweated anyway.

2
00:00:04,924 --> 00:00:08,508
"Seventy-two hours,"
the American side said.

3
00:00:08,548 --> 00:00:11,061
"Fordow is not on this agenda."

4
00:00:11,101 --> 00:00:15,102
Wars begin with gunfire, but
their real weight is often

5
00:00:15,142 --> 00:00:18,889
decided in rooms where no
one says anything at all.

6
00:00:19,089 --> 00:00:22,803
Dr. Leila Shirazi checked
the signal three times.

7
00:00:22,843 --> 00:00:28,543
The assessment read "fully neutralized."
But the signal held a regular rhythm.

8
00:00:28,583 --> 00:00:31,226
A truly dead system couldn't do that.

9
00:00:31,266 --> 00:00:35,936
The last transmission from
a source codenamed ZARRIN:

10
00:00:35,976 --> 00:00:38,819
"This is the last transmission."

11
00:00:39,019 --> 00:00:45,111
Washington's 72-hour proposal arrived
as a notification, not a consultation.

12
00:00:45,151 --> 00:00:48,551
Israel had been left out
of the Islamabad channel.

13
00:00:48,591 --> 00:00:50,817
The world read it as a warning.

14
00:00:50,857 --> 00:00:55,902
It wasn't a warning. It was the
announcement of a decision already made.

15
00:00:56,102 --> 00:01:02,011
A throat carrying a fifth of the world's
oil opened again after six days.

16
00:01:02,051 --> 00:01:06,731
"The strait's open." "Limited.
Northern lane only."

17
00:01:06,771 --> 00:01:10,538
On the horizon, the silhouette
of a tanker appeared.

18
00:01:10,578 --> 00:01:15,623
As long as Fordow's signal was
alive, the war was not over.

19
00:01:15,823 --> 00:01:21,862
Nine times Captain Kim Junho tried
to call. Nine times he stopped.

20
00:01:21,902 --> 00:01:26,087
His mother picked up on the
second ring. She'd been waiting.

21
00:01:26,127 --> 00:01:29,136
"Junho." Two syllables were enough.

22
00:01:29,176 --> 00:01:35,475
"I'm alive." "I know. Sleep
well." She asked nothing else.

23
00:01:35,675 --> 00:01:39,520
Soraya Tahir stood in the middle
of Azadi Square and sang.

24
00:01:39,560 --> 00:01:43,875
An old Persian song for the end
of winter, for flowers opening.

25
00:01:43,915 --> 00:01:48,413
One Basij member set his baton down
on the pavement and sang along.

26
00:01:48,453 --> 00:01:52,192
Spring didn't stop. Spring
is older than the war.

27
00:01:52,392 --> 00:01:59,320
Professor Azad Moradi opened the last blank
page of a notebook he'd bought in 1973.

28
00:01:59,360 --> 00:02:04,014
"Freedom is uncomfortable too.
But repression hurts longer."

29
00:02:04,054 --> 00:02:07,506
From the courtyard, the
singing rose again.

30
00:02:07,706 --> 00:02:11,734
Fordow's signal changed again.
Its strength was rising.

31
00:02:11,774 --> 00:02:17,395
"Kinetic intervention alone is not
sufficient. The next step is diplomatic."

32
00:02:17,435 --> 00:02:21,855
Bombs bring down buildings, but a
signal doesn't stop for a bomb.

33
00:02:21,895 --> 00:02:24,093
Continued in Episode 4.
